{"name":"Sedona Stone","hex":"#8e462f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sedona, Arizona","blocks":[{"text":"Sedona is a city straddling the county line between Coconino and Yavapai counties in the northern Verde Valley region of Arizona, United States. As of the 2020 census, Sedona had a population of 9,684. The city is within the Coconino National Forest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Cathedral_Rock_-_Sedona_AZ-1.jpg/330px-Cathedral_Rock_-_Sedona_AZ-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sedona%2C_Arizona","wikidata":"Q80041"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of magma in the asthenosphere. The study of rocks involves multiple subdisciplines of geology, including petrology and mineralogy. It may be limited to rocks found on Earth, or it may include planetary geology that studies the rocks of other celestial objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg/330px-Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_(geology)","wikidata":"Q8063"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Us-az-sd%29.gif/120px-Us-az-sd%29.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Us-az-sd%29.gif/250px-Us-az-sd%29.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Us-az-sd%29.gif/120px-Us-az-sd%29.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUs-az-sd).gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Chapel_of_the_Holy_Cross%2C_Sedona%2C_AZ.jpg/500px-Chapel_of_the_Holy_Cross%2C_Sedona%2C_AZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Chapel_of_the_Holy_Cross%2C_Sedona%2C_AZ.jpg/1280px-Chapel_of_the_Holy_Cross%2C_Sedona%2C_AZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Chapel_of_the_Holy_Cross%2C_Sedona%2C_AZ.jpg/500px-Chapel_of_the_Holy_Cross%2C_Sedona%2C_AZ.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Chapel of the Holy Cross","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChapel_of_the_Holy_Cross%2C_Sedona%2C_AZ.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sedona_Brins_Fire_2006.jpg/330px-Sedona_Brins_Fire_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Sedona_Brins_Fire_2006.jpg/330px-Sedona_Brins_Fire_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Brins Fire of 2006","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASedona_Brins_Fire_2006.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki